// Two-ICD coexistence test (see "Process Coexistence and Symbol
// Visibility" in feme/docs/FeMeVulkanDesign.md): the Vulkan loader loads
// *every* discovered ICD into the process, so `libfeme_vulkan.so` must
// share an address space with another, genuinely LLVM-based software
// driver (Mesa's lavapipe) without any duplicate `cl::opt` registration,
// `ManagedStatic`/target-registry collision, or RTTI/exception identity
// mismatch. Both devices must enumerate and FeMe's must still work exactly
// as it does alone.
//
// REQUIRES: system-vulkan-loader, system-second-vulkan-icd
// RUN: env VK_DRIVER_FILES=%feme_vulkan_icd_manifest:%system_second_icd_manifest \
// RUN:   VK_LOADER_DEBUG=error feme-vulkan-loader-smoke | FileCheck %s

// CHECK-DAG: found device: FeMe CPU Vulkan Device (vendorID=0x10000, apiVersion=1.4.0)
// CHECK-DAG: found device:{{.*}}(vendorID=0x10005,
// CHECK: compute queue family: {{[0-9]+}} (flags=0x{{[0-9a-f]+}})
// CHECK: PASS
